WEBVTT

00:00.260 --> 00:02.800
That witch... There's a way to save her.

00:04.460 --> 00:08.230
He wanted to be of use to someone...

00:08.230 --> 00:11.190
and if this is the only way 
that wish can come true...

00:12.720 --> 00:14.650
I hope that he'll be allowed to do so.

00:15.880 --> 00:17.400
That's something that I could see.

00:17.800 --> 00:21.410
If you hadn't been here, 
then we might have won.

00:22.090 --> 00:24.780
I'm just a handyman.

00:26.290 --> 00:31.420
<i>That world I had always envisioned</i>

00:31.420 --> 00:35.050
<i>Could I have found it?</i>

00:43.930 --> 00:48.560
<i>I lived my days at someone 
else's convenience</i>

00:48.980 --> 00:53.190
<i>Gaining nothing but compromises and regrets</i>

00:53.190 --> 00:55.320
<i>Because I always felt that</i>

00:55.320 --> 00:59.200
<i>Even if it wasn't me standing here</i>

00:59.200 --> 01:03.250
<i>The world would still keep moving forward</i>

01:03.250 --> 01:07.040
<i>Even after I lost it</i>

01:07.040 --> 01:09.340
<i>And its colors faded</i>

01:09.340 --> 01:13.420
<i>The dream from that hazily remembered day</i>

01:13.420 --> 01:15.380
<i>Still remained</i>

01:15.380 --> 01:17.800
<i>The thing that only I can do</i>

01:17.800 --> 01:20.510
<i>And the scenery that I left behind</i>

01:20.510 --> 01:28.020
<i>I was just looking for an answer 
from some other time</i>

01:29.360 --> 01:34.240
<i>Those things that don't change</i>

01:34.240 --> 01:39.820
<i>And those words I protected so carefully</i>

01:39.820 --> 01:44.450
<i>Even if they're all just 
unattractive junk to others</i>

01:44.450 --> 01:52.840
<i>They're all treasures 
that I will never give up</i>

02:00.850 --> 02:03.040
Well, they're gone.

02:03.040 --> 02:04.260
Yes.

02:04.910 --> 02:05.880
Say...

02:05.880 --> 02:08.760
did you find the thing you 
were looking for, Saitou?

02:08.760 --> 02:09.640
No.

02:10.190 --> 02:11.840
I haven't found it yet.

02:13.680 --> 02:16.940
And it's not like 
I'm focused on that specifically.

02:18.280 --> 02:21.400
Still, this place is...

02:21.790 --> 02:24.880
The magician who lived here in the past

02:24.880 --> 02:29.540
must have called these things here 
when he opened doors to other worlds.

02:30.320 --> 02:32.040
Whoa! What is all this?

02:33.310 --> 02:35.280
It's all stuff I've never seen before!

02:35.280 --> 02:36.400
Ugh.

02:36.400 --> 02:38.920
Other adventurers are coming in here.

02:38.920 --> 02:41.260
Well, the new area is popular, after all.

02:42.680 --> 02:43.970
Saitou?!

02:44.270 --> 02:46.550
I'll look for things that might be useful!

02:46.550 --> 02:48.350
I'll get them before anyone else does!

02:49.200 --> 02:50.360
I'll look too!

02:50.360 --> 02:52.050
A-And me!

02:54.750 --> 02:55.910
Master.

02:57.820 --> 03:00.840
You've regained your memories, haven't you?

03:05.820 --> 03:11.520
Hey, how long are you gonna do this for?

03:06.900 --> 03:08.250
Whoa! What is this?

03:09.150 --> 03:10.400
Hmm...

03:10.400 --> 03:11.510
This is amazing!

03:18.190 --> 03:20.840
Pemo! How have you been?

03:20.840 --> 03:24.230
It's your favorite old man!

03:21.680 --> 03:24.230
Master, you remember, don't you?

03:25.180 --> 03:27.370
That's Pemoridius II!

03:27.370 --> 03:30.970
A pup from the Pemoridius 
you loved so dearly!

03:32.440 --> 03:35.660
That means that you're...

03:36.200 --> 03:37.470
Who are you again?

03:37.470 --> 03:38.680
Hey! What's this?

03:38.680 --> 03:41.700
Oh! But I want that!

03:41.740 --> 03:45.160
<b>The Ninja and 
the Witch 
(the Conclusion)</b>

03:46.370 --> 03:47.970
Honestly.

03:47.970 --> 03:52.200
Calling the kingdom's monar— 
most wealthy man out here.

03:52.200 --> 03:56.190
Though, as it's the minister and my dear 
Demon King asking, I don't have a choice.

03:57.470 --> 04:00.670
In the room filled with magical energy 
down there, you'll find the witch.

04:04.680 --> 04:08.590
Can you really break the curse 
and restore her youth?

04:09.000 --> 04:10.060
Yes.

04:11.720 --> 04:13.730
The Spirit Returner.

04:15.030 --> 04:20.930
Also called the Blood Sword, 
it steals the life force of my enemies.

04:22.060 --> 04:24.020
You'll use that to cut me down, then?

04:24.490 --> 04:29.020
It will cost your whole life to save the witch.

04:29.020 --> 04:30.200
However...

04:30.200 --> 04:34.400
from what I've heard, you're 
an assassin who has killed many.

04:34.400 --> 04:37.960
After all of that, can you really offer 
yourself up for the sake of another?

04:39.930 --> 04:44.300
I've killed countless people
who I never knew anything about.

04:45.630 --> 04:49.720
It was my trade, and I didn't 
know any other way to live.

04:51.760 --> 04:53.920
But I found friends...

04:55.220 --> 04:57.150
and fell in love with the witch.

04:58.110 --> 04:59.990
Careful, boy.

05:00.310 --> 05:04.960
But my rash act ended up 
causing her to grow old.

05:07.840 --> 05:10.360
That's when I realized it 
for the first time.

05:11.030 --> 05:13.400
Just as I care for my friends,

05:13.400 --> 05:18.040
those I've killed must also 
have had people they loved.

05:20.320 --> 05:24.600
I have no right to love anyone.

05:25.580 --> 05:30.050
The fact that you hadn't realized 
something so simple until now...

05:30.050 --> 05:32.770
you are a pitiable man.

05:34.950 --> 05:36.900
At the very least, 
I want this sinful life...

05:37.620 --> 05:40.080
to be used to save someone.

05:40.400 --> 05:44.870
For an assassin, even that wish is selfish.

05:46.370 --> 05:49.170
However, I am magnanimous.

05:49.170 --> 05:51.400
I shall grant your wish.

05:54.800 --> 05:55.700
Please do.

07:37.790 --> 07:40.520
The Spirit Returner has begun to glow.

07:41.150 --> 07:43.280
Just a little more, I think.

07:44.150 --> 07:47.360
What is needed for this magic...

07:47.360 --> 07:51.770
is the life of someone who knows 
the one whose youth will be restored.

07:53.160 --> 07:58.470
I'll use yours and that 
black fairy's lives, half of each.

07:59.760 --> 08:01.370
Primasse's wings?!

08:02.800 --> 08:05.840
Until this sword glows crimson,

08:05.840 --> 08:08.290
I shall continue to cut you into pieces.

08:08.970 --> 08:10.800
Do you understand?

08:44.230 --> 08:47.290
Who... are you?

08:56.560 --> 08:57.980
I'm sorry.

08:57.980 --> 09:01.080
I've been asleep for a long time.

09:01.080 --> 09:04.040
I don't have anything to offer you.

09:04.560 --> 09:05.760
I see.

09:30.500 --> 09:31.840
This is for the best.

09:31.840 --> 09:33.590
Coward!

09:34.200 --> 09:37.090
Are you planning to just leave like this, 
like nothing happened?

09:37.090 --> 09:38.840
It's all right, Primasse.

09:38.840 --> 09:42.350
Just the fact that she's back 
to what she was makes me...

09:42.350 --> 09:43.430
It's not all right!

09:44.030 --> 09:45.650
What's going to happen to me?

09:45.650 --> 09:48.420
I offered up my wings. Plus, 
all my magic was sucked out of me!

09:48.420 --> 09:50.440
I've gotten all skinny again!

09:50.440 --> 09:52.640
I won't let you leave like this!

09:52.640 --> 09:54.830
So what if she doesn't have her memories?

09:54.830 --> 09:57.440
If you're a real man, 
then go and win her over!

09:57.440 --> 09:59.920
But I'm an assassin.

09:59.920 --> 10:02.990
I shouldn't be allowed to be happy.

10:01.290 --> 10:02.990
Stop making excuses!

10:02.990 --> 10:05.400
The moment you sprang into action 
for the woman you loved,

10:05.400 --> 10:07.630
you were already being selfish, you villain!

10:07.630 --> 10:10.080
You lived in a kill-or-be-killed world!

10:10.080 --> 10:11.880
Why are you saying all this for now?

10:11.880 --> 10:14.680
What are you planning 
to do next? Become a monk?

10:14.680 --> 10:17.360
It's impossible! You could 
never learn holy magic now!

10:17.360 --> 10:19.680
If your alternative is 
to memorize some useless charms,

10:19.680 --> 10:22.000
then go and prove that you 
can make one woman happy!

10:23.800 --> 10:25.800
Just be still!

10:28.440 --> 10:30.240
What's it gonna hurt?

10:30.240 --> 10:32.180
We've lost our way, see?

10:32.180 --> 10:34.060
Let us rest here a while.

10:34.060 --> 10:36.440
She should be able to 
handle minor thugs like that.

10:36.440 --> 10:39.620
But I didn't sense much 
magical energy earlier.

10:39.620 --> 10:40.520
What?

10:40.520 --> 10:43.360
And she's only just woken up, after all.

10:40.840 --> 10:42.760
C'mon. Let us in.

10:43.640 --> 10:44.990
Blast it!

10:46.380 --> 10:48.840
Hey, you don't mind, right?

10:50.500 --> 10:52.720
Step away from the lady.

10:52.720 --> 10:54.990
Who're you? Quit interfering!

10:54.990 --> 10:57.080
You wanna get killed?

10:58.680 --> 11:01.720
This guy... Even with his 
body like that, he's strong!

11:01.720 --> 11:02.510
Crap!

11:05.720 --> 11:07.560
H-Hey, look! He's falling over!

11:09.800 --> 11:11.440
I can't move!

11:11.440 --> 11:16.050
Anyone whose shadow I step 
on has their every movement sealed away.

11:16.050 --> 11:16.900
Wha?!

11:16.900 --> 11:21.400
Even with a body like this, 
I'm capable of slitting your throat!

11:22.920 --> 11:24.830
W-We're very sorry!

11:26.830 --> 11:29.540
Though I won't be killing anymore.

11:29.540 --> 11:30.780
Thank you.

11:36.400 --> 11:38.850
He saved you, and that's all you've got?

11:38.850 --> 11:40.600
What an ungrateful woman.

11:43.220 --> 11:45.920
The smell of wheat is pouring out of there.

11:45.920 --> 11:47.880
You bake sweets, don't you?

11:47.880 --> 11:49.100
Treat us to something.

11:49.100 --> 11:51.040
Then we'll call it even.

11:51.040 --> 11:52.160
Hey!

11:52.160 --> 11:54.110
Right, Kisurugi?

11:55.260 --> 11:57.040
Y-Yes.

11:57.650 --> 11:59.600
If it isn't an imposition.

12:02.060 --> 12:03.860
You two are strange.

12:04.200 --> 12:06.950
Come in. I'll show you my gratitude.

12:08.240 --> 12:09.780
Would you like a hand?

12:09.780 --> 12:11.000
No.

12:17.480 --> 12:19.090
Honestly.

12:19.600 --> 12:23.170
Boss wouldn't have the courage unless we did this.

12:23.560 --> 12:27.180
I was scared he might 
suddenly kiss her again, though.

12:30.080 --> 12:34.220
<i>The ninja and the witch will
surely fall in love again.</i>

12:39.020 --> 12:42.440
<b>Returning from 
the Great Labyrinth</b>

12:39.020 --> 12:42.440
<b>Returning</b>

12:45.210 --> 12:48.370
These are all items which are prohibited 
from being taken away.

12:49.830 --> 12:51.280
The royal magician...

12:51.730 --> 12:53.390
will be looking into all of these.

12:54.650 --> 12:57.170
And when we'd managed 
to carry them all out, too.

12:57.510 --> 13:01.560
In the end, we never did find 
that robot vacuum, though.

13:01.560 --> 13:03.590
Is it really so valuable?

13:03.590 --> 13:04.280
Yes.

13:04.280 --> 13:08.280
It might even be capable of changing 
this world's whole civilization, but...

13:08.280 --> 13:09.920
it doesn't really matter.

13:09.920 --> 13:11.220
What's more important...

13:11.620 --> 13:12.600
Everyone...

13:20.090 --> 13:22.600
Thank you for coming to our rescue.

13:22.600 --> 13:25.610
I was simply concerned 
for my master's safety.

13:25.610 --> 13:27.110
Who was that again?

13:27.110 --> 13:28.570
Armored Warrior,

13:28.570 --> 13:31.610
the one who will defeat you is me, 
Flanril, understand?

13:32.240 --> 13:33.830
I'm ready any time.

13:36.240 --> 13:37.890
There's no need for thanks.

13:37.890 --> 13:41.260
After all, Guivre here loves 
that Saitou, you know?

13:41.260 --> 13:44.000
Is that really something 
you should say now? Here?

13:47.760 --> 13:50.510
A thank you goes to the kingdom's 
officially recognized hero, too!

13:50.510 --> 13:52.590
As the hero, it was only natural!

13:52.590 --> 13:54.760
...is what I'd like to say, but...

13:54.760 --> 13:57.640
Monpui here was worried 
for Master Saitou!

13:57.640 --> 13:59.850
No, I wasn't really.

13:59.850 --> 14:02.360
Well, I didn't want to,

14:02.360 --> 14:04.030
but Monpui kept insisting.

14:02.960 --> 14:04.830
No, as I said, I wasn't...

14:04.030 --> 14:05.780
Well, I'm sure we'll run 
into each other again.

14:06.080 --> 14:07.860
Thank you! Really!

14:08.200 --> 14:09.480
See you later.

14:16.770 --> 14:18.350
They're all gone.

14:18.600 --> 14:21.750
If we head down into the great labyrinth, 
we can see them whenever we want.

14:22.420 --> 14:23.710
Well...

14:23.710 --> 14:26.120
Shall we go get some rest at the inn?

14:26.720 --> 14:28.840
I'm starving!

14:28.840 --> 14:31.280
I'd like to rest my back.

14:31.280 --> 14:31.960
Wait.

14:32.200 --> 14:34.200
Wait, we need to talk before that.

14:36.320 --> 14:37.640
Raelza?

14:38.220 --> 14:39.930
Is it really true?

14:40.400 --> 14:43.710
Did the geezer really 
call Saitou to this world?

14:45.280 --> 14:48.700
<b>The Possibility 
of Returning</b>

14:51.760 --> 14:52.750
Then...

14:52.750 --> 14:55.000
that means, without even realizing it,

14:55.000 --> 14:59.750
you used magic that opened 
a door to another world?

14:59.750 --> 15:01.120
That's right.

15:01.120 --> 15:04.250
Within the memories I've lost...

15:04.370 --> 15:09.500
There's someone I wanted to see 
more than anything, you see?

15:10.000 --> 15:14.520
I can't remember who it was I wanted to see,

15:15.160 --> 15:16.510
but that morning...

15:16.870 --> 15:21.760
I tried to use that magic and failed. 
I remember that now.

15:25.530 --> 15:26.280
Don't kill him!

15:26.280 --> 15:29.770
When I arrived, Saitou was there.

15:29.770 --> 15:31.430
Which means...

15:31.430 --> 15:34.540
I was accidentally 
called here by that magic?

15:34.540 --> 15:36.270
I'm sorry.

15:36.270 --> 15:39.430
That's all I know right now.

15:39.430 --> 15:41.730
No, it's all right, Morlock-san.

15:41.730 --> 15:43.540
Thanks to that, I...

15:43.540 --> 15:47.000
I wasn't hit by a truck... 
um, a large vehicle.

15:49.590 --> 15:52.130
Actually, you could say 
that you saved my life, in a way.

15:53.520 --> 15:56.120
Saitou...

15:58.090 --> 16:01.550
Say, if that's true, Grandpa, then...

16:01.920 --> 16:04.290
Couldn't you open 
that door to another world...

16:04.290 --> 16:08.070
and send Saitou back 
to the world he came from?

16:11.630 --> 16:13.640
The world I came from?

16:13.640 --> 16:14.440
No!

16:15.030 --> 16:16.950
You can't do that!

16:16.950 --> 16:18.700
What about exploring?

16:18.700 --> 16:20.160
Raelza...

16:20.620 --> 16:23.440
How was it when Saitou 
wasn't around because of a cold?

16:23.440 --> 16:26.590
And in the fight with the ninja, too...

16:26.590 --> 16:31.340
You know that this party's reputation only 
started to rise after Saitou joined us!

16:31.340 --> 16:33.580
Return to the world he came from?

16:33.580 --> 16:36.000
How could that be all right?

16:42.120 --> 16:43.450
Raelza!

16:45.570 --> 16:47.560
Raelza!

16:48.210 --> 16:50.020
Saitou!

16:50.340 --> 16:52.520
Ugh, where did they go?

16:52.520 --> 16:55.200
Monsters appear around here, you know?

16:55.200 --> 16:58.120
And Raelza went and left her sword behind.

17:08.800 --> 17:12.090
Do you want to go back 
to the world you came from?

17:12.550 --> 17:15.430
We still don't know if I can go back.

17:15.430 --> 17:21.050
Besides, no one needed me in that world.

17:21.050 --> 17:24.560
You don't have family or anything?

17:24.560 --> 17:28.550
I do have family, but I haven't
 seen them for years.

17:28.550 --> 17:32.940
It'd be a lie to say I don't 
miss them at all, but...

17:34.070 --> 17:35.350
Raelza...

17:35.350 --> 17:40.540
Earlier, when you said I was useful 
to the party, it made me happy.

17:41.460 --> 17:43.540
It may just be conceit on my part,

17:43.540 --> 17:46.200
but I feel like this, right now,

17:46.200 --> 17:49.050
is the most I've ever 
been needed in my life.

17:53.640 --> 17:56.210
Raelza, do you need me?

18:03.640 --> 18:06.220
Saitou, I...

18:11.150 --> 18:12.730
What I feel for you is...

18:17.780 --> 18:19.370
Raelza! A monster!

18:24.190 --> 18:25.290
Raelza!

18:30.280 --> 18:32.580
An armored serpent...

18:32.870 --> 18:34.060
Rae—

18:40.920 --> 18:42.350
Saitou...

18:42.350 --> 18:43.800
Raelza...

18:48.740 --> 18:52.990
Earlier, I said that our party needed you...

18:55.700 --> 18:57.560
but the truth is...

18:58.600 --> 19:01.170
the one who needs you most in this world...

19:01.170 --> 19:02.560
No.

19:02.560 --> 19:06.080
More than if you added everyone 
in the world you came from, too.

19:06.800 --> 19:08.500
More than anyone!

19:16.730 --> 19:18.340
More than anyone else...

19:18.350 --> 19:20.510
I need you.

19:34.000 --> 19:36.190
It caught you a little, didn't it?

19:36.510 --> 19:39.070
The armored serpent has venom in its claws.

19:39.070 --> 19:40.750
It takes effect later.

19:41.340 --> 19:43.200
We can't have you getting a scar here.

19:43.200 --> 19:45.250
Let's put some magical medicine on it.

19:48.410 --> 19:51.240
Drink this anti-venom, too.

20:02.640 --> 20:07.800
I want to be with 
the person who needs me the most.

20:17.990 --> 20:19.790
Saitou!

20:19.790 --> 20:22.820
You've gotten quite knowledgeable 
about monsters, too.

20:22.820 --> 20:24.480
Geezer?

20:24.480 --> 20:27.830
The shell of an armored 
serpent sells for a high price!

20:29.590 --> 20:33.000
So, geezer, what about what we 
were discussing earlier?

20:33.490 --> 20:34.710
Can you do it?

20:36.200 --> 20:38.800
Don't tilt your head like that. 
It's not endearing.

20:38.800 --> 20:40.140
It seems like he's forgotten.

20:41.260 --> 20:44.090
If it's true that you summoned Saitou here,

20:44.090 --> 20:46.270
can you do the reverse?

20:46.270 --> 20:49.480
Well, about that...

20:49.480 --> 20:51.140
Have you forgotten how?

20:51.140 --> 20:54.960
If I had the book of magic, 
I might be able to.

20:54.960 --> 20:57.510
But even if I did successfully manage it...

20:58.040 --> 20:59.520
If you did, then...

20:59.760 --> 21:01.270
Saitou...

21:01.270 --> 21:03.760
in that world, you said a trukk,

21:03.760 --> 21:08.500
some large vehicle, 
was about to hit you, right?

21:08.500 --> 21:09.530
Yes. Why?

21:10.030 --> 21:11.990
You can't mean... Grandpa?

21:11.990 --> 21:13.240
That's right.

21:13.650 --> 21:16.400
Even if the magic succeeds...

21:16.400 --> 21:20.800
since Saitou will be returned 
to that exact same place and time...

21:21.580 --> 21:24.640
If I go back to the world 
I came from, I'll die?

21:24.640 --> 21:26.510
Saitou...

21:29.200 --> 21:32.320
Well, it's not like I'm planning to go back,

21:32.320 --> 21:33.600
so I guess it doesn't matter.

21:36.940 --> 21:39.240
Which means, I hope you'll continue to—

21:40.100 --> 21:42.650
Oh. The armored serpent was still alive.

21:42.650 --> 21:45.810
The area around my shoulders 
feels a little itchy.

21:45.810 --> 21:48.440
Geezer, don't tilt your head like that.

21:48.440 --> 21:51.930
I can't use any magic 
that works on this venom.

21:51.930 --> 21:55.190
And I used up the magical medicine earlier.

21:56.620 --> 22:00.040
<b>And So, Back to 
the Routine Life 
of an Adventurer</b>

22:10.080 --> 22:11.650
Morning!

22:11.650 --> 22:14.820
Isn't it great that Saitou decided to stay?

22:16.350 --> 22:19.360
<i>Like being gently carried away on a current</i>

22:17.120 --> 22:18.650
<i>Our party...</i>

22:18.650 --> 22:20.560
<i>will go exploring again today.</i>

22:19.360 --> 22:22.250
<i>Like drifting off to sleep at night</i>

22:21.440 --> 22:24.070
<i>Just like farmers harvesting their wheat...</i>

22:22.250 --> 22:24.240
<i>Like there's nothing 
particularly special about it</i>

22:24.240 --> 22:26.380
<i>Our hearts are one</i>

22:24.810 --> 22:27.070
<i>Just like hunters stalking deer...</i>

22:26.380 --> 22:29.320
<i>“See you later” illuminates the way</i>

22:27.300 --> 22:29.320
<i>we'll earn our daily wages in these caves.</i>

22:29.320 --> 22:31.240
<i>To the depths of the future</i>

22:31.240 --> 22:36.240
<i>Where kindness is the one 
thing I'm certain I felt</i>

22:36.240 --> 22:37.780
<i>Saitou...</i>

22:36.240 --> 22:41.000
<i>You know, I'm sure we 
don't know anything</i>

22:37.780 --> 22:40.550
<i>I've told you that I need you.</i>

22:40.920 --> 22:41.870
What about you?

22:41.000 --> 22:45.910
<i>But you know, for right now, that’s fine</i>

22:42.440 --> 22:45.980
You haven't clearly stated 
what your feelings are.

22:45.910 --> 22:48.680
<i>I'm waiting, I'm waiting</i>

22:47.520 --> 22:50.080
But...that's all right for now.

22:48.680 --> 22:50.900
<i>Let's sing here again</i>

22:50.450 --> 22:52.290
Someday, please tell me.

22:50.900 --> 22:53.680
<i>One day, we'll shine the light</i>

22:53.680 --> 22:56.360
<i>Now, I think I can embrace even my tears</i>

22:55.310 --> 22:58.430
On the upper floors, it's easier 
without the geezer, isn't it?

22:56.360 --> 22:58.450
<i>As we picture it, as we paint it</i>

22:58.430 --> 23:00.370
Hmm. You might be right.

22:58.450 --> 23:00.590
<i>A single bit of warmth is all there is</i>

23:00.370 --> 23:04.240
Since he's resting today because of 
that venom yesterday, it's perfect, isn't it?

23:00.590 --> 23:07.010
<i>And now, so that we can 
laugh, let's hold hands</i>

23:06.960 --> 23:09.360
I never imagined it would take us four days.

23:07.010 --> 23:12.930
<i>That’s right, it will 
blossom in the skies</i>

23:09.360 --> 23:12.120
Well, it is an area with no map.

23:12.120 --> 23:14.870
If Morlock-san had been with us, 
we might have been able to leave right away.

23:12.930 --> 23:19.140
<i>A guidepost showing us the way to live</i>

23:15.320 --> 23:17.950
That's our punishment 
for making fun of Grandpa.

23:17.950 --> 23:21.880
I suppose it means
the geezer's more useful than a bug.

23:23.030 --> 23:25.250
We're back. Are you feeling—

23:25.960 --> 23:26.710
Huh?

23:27.030 --> 23:28.400
Geezer?

23:30.530 --> 23:32.000
Why isn't he here?

23:32.320 --> 23:33.470
Excuse me.

23:35.110 --> 23:37.600
About the guest in that room...

23:37.600 --> 23:38.470
What?

23:40.750 --> 23:42.460
Three days ago...

23:42.460 --> 23:44.370
he passed away.

23:46.110 --> 23:49.990
<b>To Be Continued!</b>
